    cash_conversion_cycle: "Wave 7, 2026-08-24: declared in the schema and read by the nightly fundamentals pass, but NEVER YET WRITTEN by a production build -- so under R8 it cannot be a scalar yet. A column no build has filled would make every expression over it silently NULL, which reads to a member as a screen that found nothing rather than a vocabulary that holds nothing. PROMOTE IT after a clean nightly fill shows real coverage, exactly as pattern_engine_vcp and pattern_engine_flat_base were promoted the same day they filled -- and move only the split, never the column total.",
    candle_label: "TEXT -- the wording the Candle column displays: the bar's named shape, with the runner-up in parentheses. A name is not a magnitude. The measured parts of that same bar are declared as scalars instead: body as a fraction of range (body_pct), the two wicks (upper_wick_pct, lower_wick_pct) and where it closed (close_position).",
    candle_matches: "TEXT -- every named shape the newest bar satisfied at once, delimiter-wrapped so the Candle Type filter can test membership. A list is not a number and this grammar has no string literal, so no expression over it is writeable. The measured parts of that same bar are declared as scalars instead: body_pct, upper_wick_pct, lower_wick_pct and close_position.",
    candle_trend: "TEXT -- the Prior Trend the candle printed into (up, down, neutral or unknown), read from a 10-day EMA at the bar before the pattern begins. It is a verdict, not a magnitude, and it has no numeric part: no column stores the slope or the distance behind the verdict.",
    bar_character: "TEXT -- the Bar Character headline: what the newest bar DID, one of 53 behaviours across gaps, structural failures, reversals and volume, decided by a strict priority cascade. A headline is not a magnitude. The facts it is built from are declared as scalars where they are stored as numbers: the gap (gap_pct), volume against its average (vol_ratio), whether the range was wide or narrow against ATR (wide_bar, narrow_bar) and where the bar closed (close_position). The 20-day high and low tests and the gap-filled verdict are not stored as columns.",
    bar_character_label: "TEXT -- the wording the Character column displays: the headline plus where the bar closed and how heavy the volume was. Prose, not a magnitude, and it carries no number of its own: the gap (gap_pct), the volume ratio (vol_ratio), a wide or narrow range (wide_bar, narrow_bar) and the close position (close_position) it describes are the declared scalars.",
    candle_recent: "TEXT -- the name of the Recent Pattern: the most recent multi-bar structure inside the last five sessions. A name is not a magnitude; its numeric part, how many sessions ago it completed, is declared as candle_recent_bars_ago.",
    candle_recent_label: "TEXT -- the wording the Recent Pattern column displays: the name, its age and what the next open did. Prose, not a magnitude; the one number inside it, the age in sessions, is declared as candle_recent_bars_ago.",
    candle_recent_status: "TEXT -- Next Open After Pattern: whether the session after the Recent Pattern opened with it or against it, or provisional while no session has opened since. It is a direction, not a magnitude, and it has no numeric part: the size of that opening gap is not stored, only which side of the pattern's close it fell on.",
    candle_weekly: "TEXT -- the Weekly Candle: the named shape of the weekly bar, resampled from the daily series. A name is not a magnitude, and it has no numeric part: the weekly bar's body, wicks and close position are computed to name it and not stored as columns. Only the DAILY bar's measurements are declared (body_pct, upper_wick_pct, lower_wick_pct, close_position).",
    candle_weekly_label: "TEXT -- the wording the Weekly column displays, including the (forming) flag while the week is still open. Prose, not a magnitude, and it has no numeric part: nothing about the weekly bar is stored as a number.",
    candle_monthly: "TEXT -- the Monthly Candle: the named shape of the monthly bar, resampled from the daily series. A name is not a magnitude, and it has no numeric part: the monthly bar's body, wicks and close position are computed to name it and not stored as columns. Only the DAILY bar's measurements are declared (body_pct, upper_wick_pct, lower_wick_pct, close_position).",
    candle_monthly_label: "TEXT -- the wording the Monthly column displays, including the (forming) flag while the month is still open. Prose, not a magnitude, and it has no numeric part: nothing about the monthly bar is stored as a number.",
    base_shape: "TEXT -- the trend structure's machine key. A classification label is not a number and this grammar has no string literal, so no expression over it is writeable. The countable part, `base_relation_count`, IS declared",
    base_shape_label: "TEXT -- the display form of `base_shape`, carried so the grid can render a label without a second lookup",
    base_matches: "TEXT -- every structure the symbol satisfied at once, delimiter-wrapped so the Base Structure filter can test membership. A list is not a number; expressing membership needs a `contains` this table does not declare, exactly as `patterns` and `candle_matches` already record",
    base_render: "TEXT -- the rendered head, primary (secondary) +N. A display string, not a fact a formula can compute over",
    rvol_live: "LIVE-ONLY -- volume vs usual by now, written only by the screener's intraday overlay and NULL in every nightly row by design. A scalar is read from `screener_rows` at the snapshot's cadence, so every expression over it would be a hole on every symbol at every hour; the nightly volume reading a formula can use is `vol_ratio`",
    archive_calls_n: "DISPLAY-ONLY ARCHIVE CONTEXT, 2026-10-16 -- written by `archive_join` from the private trader archive and refused as a scalar on purpose: owner decision 3 allows archive context on scanner surfaces only as DISPLAY, never as an input to what fires or how it scores, and a declared scalar would let a formula, a saved scan or an alert condition key on it. It is also blank whenever WISDOM_ARCHIVE_ENABLED is off, so under R8 it cannot be one yet either",
    archive_traders_n: "DISPLAY-ONLY ARCHIVE CONTEXT, 2026-10-16 -- written by `archive_join` from the private trader archive and refused as a scalar on purpose: owner decision 3 allows archive context on scanner surfaces only as DISPLAY, never as an input to what fires or how it scores, and a declared scalar would let a formula, a saved scan or an alert condition key on it. It is also blank whenever WISDOM_ARCHIVE_ENABLED is off, so under R8 it cannot be one yet either",
    archive_last_call_date: "TEXT -- the date of the team's newest archived call on the name. DISPLAY-ONLY ARCHIVE CONTEXT, 2026-10-16 -- written by `archive_join` from the private trader archive and refused as a scalar on purpose: owner decision 3 allows archive context on scanner surfaces only as DISPLAY, never as an input to what fires or how it scores, and a declared scalar would let a formula, a saved scan or an alert condition key on it. It is also blank whenever WISDOM_ARCHIVE_ENABLED is off, so under R8 it cannot be one yet either",
